## Context

Spun out of the 0602 investigation (author: "if coherence.py is dead why
keep it?"). `src/aedist/coherence.py` (check_row_coherence,
check_cross_row_coherence, check_aggregate_coherence, check_coherence) is
a v1 table-based coherence module that the PRODUCTION scorer does not
call — `score_mechanical.py:score_coherence` + `score_coherence_level.py`
do the real coherence scoring. The only importer of `aedist.coherence` is
its own `tests/test_coherence.py` (no `src/` file imports it).

## Actions

1. Confirm dead: `grep -rn 'aedist.coherence\|from .coherence import\|import coherence'
   src/ experiments/` → expect zero production importers (only
   tests/test_coherence.py). Verify the scorer path
   (score_mechanical/score_coherence_level) does not depend on it.
2. If confirmed unused in production: delete `src/aedist/coherence.py`
   AND `tests/test_coherence.py`. (A test that exists only to test dead
   code is also dead.)
3. If anything DOES depend on it that the grep missed, do not delete —
   instead add a module docstring explaining why it is retained, and
   report the dependency.
4. `make check` must stay green after removal (the ruff-adherence + full
   suite).

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/coherence.py` (remove), `tests/test_coherence.py` (remove).

## Verification

- [ ] Zero production importers of `aedist.coherence` (re-confirmed).
- [ ] Module + its test removed (or retained-with-docstring if a real
      dependency surfaces).
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Exit criteria

- Dead v1 coherence module gone (or justified in a docstring); `make
  check` green.
